From: Richard DEMONGEOT <richard@rdem-systems.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 07:46:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 121/123] gui: enable or disable a scheduled job (issue #17)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A "Job enabled" checkbox in the schedule form, between the daily time and
"Also run at machine startup". The scheduler already skipped jobs with
enabled=false, but SaveScheduledJob forced it to true and
UpdateScheduledJob kept the stored value, so the flag could only be
changed by editing scheduled_jobs.json. Both now store it as sent.

Disabled jobs are greyed out with a "Disabled" badge in the job list.
"Run now" still runs them on demand.

HTTP API callers that send no "enabled" key keep the old behaviour: a
created job is enabled, an updated job keeps its stored state.

Suggested by Tácio Andrade (@Tacioandrade).
